# Mechanism: widget-catalog

command: python3 -B scripts/check-widget-catalog.py CAT-001
inputs:
  - .cairn/mechanisms
  - Cargo.toml
  - Cargo.lock
  - build.rs
  - src
  - crates
  - reactive-tui-macros
  - examples
  - manual/assets/logo.jpg
  - README.md
  - manual/README.md
  - scripts
  - tests
requirements:
  - CAT-001

The check MUST first prove its validator rejects a missing widget-family page,
an external or wrong logo asset, compile-only evidence, identical animation
frames, and a quit sequence that leaves the example running.

The shell check runs the catalog behavior tests and locked example compile.
Motion and media failures belong to their own mechanisms, not this result.
